      <p class="_abstract">Pod priority uses priority classes with integer values to determine scheduling order, with higher-priority pods placed ahead in the queue and scheduled before lower-priority pods when requirements are met.</p>
      <h3 id="admin-guide-priority-preemption-priority-class_nodes-pods-priority" class="group scroll-mt-20">Pod priority classes<a href="#admin-guide-priority-preemption-priority-class_nodes-pods-priority" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>You can assign pods a priority class, which is a non-namespaced object that defines a mapping from a name to the integer value of the priority. The higher the value, the higher the priority.</p>
